quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  6,147,"If they reject you, say: ‘Your Lord is the Possessor of an expansive mercy, yet His punishment will not be averted from the wicked people.’"
  6,148,"The polytheists will say: ‘If Allah had willed, we would not have ascribed partners (to Him), nor our fathers, nor would we have forbidden anything.’ In the same way, those who were before them had continually rejected (the truth) until they tasted Our punishment. Say: ‘Do you have any (revealed) knowledge that you can produce before us? You follow nothing except (false) assumptions, and you do nothing but lie.’"
  6,149,"Say: ‘To Allah belongs the conclusive argument. If Allah had wished, He would have surely guided you all.’*"
  6,150,"Say: ‘Bring your witnesses who may testify that Allah has forbidden this.’ So if they (falsely) testify, do not testify with them, and do not follow the desires of those who have rejected Our revelations, and those who do not believe in the Hereafter and have set up equals with their Lord."
  6,151,"Say: ‘Come! I will recite (to you) what your Lord has forbidden you from. That you should not ascribe anything as a partner to Him; that you should be virtuous to (your) parents; that you should not kill your children fearing poverty—We will provide for you and for them—that you should not come near indecencies, the outward among them or the inward; and that you should not kill any soul that Allah has made inviolable, except through lawful means. That is what He has commanded you so that you may understand.’"
